# Take off, then roll left and keep turning: the landscape and the sky are drawn at an angle.
# Rolled, the sky's one-texel-per-line strips become long thin diagonal texels (filled as spans).
description: new game, take off, roll and turn (rotated landscape and sky)
suite: full
frames: 2200
performance: yes
expect: first('status', 1, 700) is not None
expect: at(1700)['zrot'] == 0 and at(1700)['status'] == 1
expect: min(col('zrot', 1800, 2200)) > 200000
expect: at(2200)['xrot'] != at(1800)['xrot']
expect: last['lives'] == 3 and last['shields'] == 64
script:
300 304 DOWN
330 336 A
480 486 A
600 606 A
760 766 A
900 906 A
1100 1106 A
1300 1500 A
1700 1760 LEFT
